---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
import ToolPrivacy from '../../components/ToolPrivacy.astro';
import ToolOthers from '../../components/ToolOthers.astro';
const years = [1, 2, 3];
---
<Base
  title="Campus data rate calculator"
  description="Turn up to three years of reported campus incident counts into rates per 1,000 students, with the caveats on reporting, Clery geography and comparison that must travel with them."
  eyebrow="Tools"
  lede="Enter counts of reported incidents for up to three years and an enrollment figure. The tool gives rates per 1,000 students, and the caveats that go with them."
>
  <h2 id="what-it-does">What it does</h2>
  <p>
    Campus safety figures, such as those in an Annual Security Report under the Clery Act, are counts. A count is
    hard to read on its own: 30 reports means something different at a college of 2,000 students than at one of
    30,000. This tool divides each year’s count by enrollment and multiplies by 1,000, so the years can be read on the
    same scale.
  </p>
  <div class="tool-caveats" role="note" aria-labelledby="cr-caveats-title">
    <p id="cr-caveats-title">Read before using the numbers</p>
    <ul>
      <li>Reported incidents depend on reporting. A rise can mean more incidents, more confidence in reporting, a new reporting channel, or a change in how cases are counted. A fall can mean the reverse.</li>
      <li>Clery counts cover a defined geography: campus, certain non-campus buildings, and adjacent public property. Incidents elsewhere, including many off-campus residences, are not counted.</li>
      <li>Do not compare raw counts, or these rates, across institutions. Geography, reporting cultures, student populations and recording practices differ.</li>
      <li>Climate surveys measure prevalence (how many students say something happened to them), usually by survey sample and over a different period. Survey figures and reported counts measure different things and do not check each other.</li>
      <li>Enrollment is only a rough denominator. Counts include incidents involving staff, visitors and people with no link to the institution.</li>
    </ul>
  </div>
  <p>More context: the <a href="/campus-safety/">campus safety record</a> and the <a href="/law/">law explainers</a>.</p>
  <ToolPrivacy />

  <h2 id="calculator">The calculator</h2>
  <p data-no-js class="tool-nojs">
    JavaScript is off, so the calculator is hidden. To work out a rate by hand: divide the count by enrollment and
    multiply by 1,000. For example, 30 reports at an enrollment of 20,000 is 30 ÷ 20,000 × 1,000 = 1.5 per 1,000 students.
  </p>
  <form class="tool" id="cr-form" data-js-only hidden novalidate aria-label="Rate calculator">
    <fieldset class="tool-fields">
      <legend>What you are counting</legend>
      <div class="tool-field">
        <label for="cr-category">Category (optional)</label>
        <input id="cr-category" name="category" type="text" autocomplete="off" placeholder="For example: rape, Clery, on campus" />
      </div>
      <div class="tool-field">
        <label for="cr-enrollment">Enrollment</label>
        <input id="cr-enrollment" name="enrollment" type="text" inputmode="numeric" autocomplete="off" aria-describedby="cr-enrollment-hint" required />
        <span class="hint" id="cr-enrollment-hint">Total students, from the same institution and a matching year.</span>
      </div>
    </fieldset>
    <fieldset class="tool-fields">
      <legend>Reported incidents, up to three years</legend>
      {years.map((n) => (
        <>
          <div class="tool-field">
            <label for={`cr-year-${n}`}>Year {n}</label>
            <input id={`cr-year-${n}`} name={`year-${n}`} type="text" inputmode="numeric" autocomplete="off" placeholder={String(2021 + n)} />
          </div>
          <div class="tool-field">
            <label for={`cr-count-${n}`}>Count for year {n}</label>
            <input id={`cr-count-${n}`} name={`count-${n}`} type="text" inputmode="numeric" autocomplete="off" />
          </div>
        </>
      ))}
      <p class="hint tool-field wide" style="margin:0">Leave a count blank to leave that year out. Enter 0 for a year with no reported incidents.</p>
    </fieldset>
    <div class="tool-actions">
      <button type="reset" class="tool-btn">Clear</button>
    </div>
  </form>

  <section class="tool-result" data-js-only hidden aria-labelledby="cr-result-title">
    <h3 id="cr-result-title">Rates per 1,000 students</h3>
    <p class="tool-status" role="status" aria-live="polite" id="cr-status">Enter an enrollment figure and at least one count.</p>
    <div id="cr-detail"></div>
    <div class="tool-output" id="cr-out" hidden>
      <h4>As plain text</h4>
      <pre id="cr-text" tabindex="0" aria-label="The rates as plain text"></pre>
      <div class="tool-copy"><button type="button" class="tool-btn" data-copy="cr-text">Copy text</button><span data-copy-status aria-live="polite"></span></div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <h2 id="how-this-works">How this works</h2>
  <p>Rate per 1,000 students = reported incidents ÷ enrollment × 1,000, shown to two decimal places.</p>
  <ul>
    <li>Counts must be whole numbers of 0 or more. Commas are allowed (1,250). A blank count leaves the year out; a zero is kept, and shown as zero reported, not zero occurred.</li>
    <li>Enrollment must be a whole number of at least 1. The same figure is used for every year, so if enrollment changed, run the calculator once for each year with that year’s enrollment.</li>
    <li>Years are optional labels. Use a four-digit year or an academic year such as 2023–24.</li>
    <li>The tool warns when counts are small (under 10), when a count exceeds enrollment, and when enrollment is under 1,000.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>The logic is in <code>src/lib/tools/campus-rates.ts</code> and is unit-tested.</p>
  <ToolOthers current="/tools/campus-rates/" />

  <script>
    import { computeRates, formatRate, ratesReport } from '../../lib/tools/campus-rates';
    import { enhance, readForm, h, list, render, wireCopy } from '../../scripts/tool-ui';

    const form = document.querySelector<HTMLFormElement>('#cr-form');
    const status = document.getElementById('cr-status');
    const detail = document.getElementById('cr-detail');
    const out = document.getElementById('cr-out');
    const text = document.getElementById('cr-text');
    if (form && status && detail && out && text) {
      enhance();
      wireCopy();
      const inputs = [...form.querySelectorAll<HTMLInputElement>('input[name]')];
      const run = () => {
        const v = readForm(form);
        const anyEntered = inputs.some((i) => i.name !== 'category' && i.value.trim());
        const r = computeRates({ enrollment: v.enrollment ?? '', category: v.category, years: [1, 2, 3].map((n) => ({ label: v[`year-${n}`] ?? '', count: v[`count-${n}`] ?? '' })) });
        const bad = new Set(r.errors.map((e) => e.field));
        for (const i of inputs) {
          const invalid = anyEntered && bad.has(i.name);
          if (invalid) i.setAttribute('aria-invalid', 'true'); else i.removeAttribute('aria-invalid');
        }
        if (!anyEntered) {
          status.textContent = 'Enter an enrollment figure and at least one count.';
          render(detail); out.hidden = true; return;
        }
        if (r.errors.length) {
          status.textContent = r.errors.length === 1 ? 'One entry needs fixing.' : `${r.errors.length} entries need fixing.`;
          render(detail, list(r.errors.map((e) => e.message), 'tool-errors'));
          out.hidden = true; return;
        }
        status.textContent = r.rows.map((x) => `${x.label}: ${formatRate(x.rate)} per 1,000`).join('; ') + '.';
        render(detail,
          h('div', { class: 'table-wrap tool-rates' }, h('table', {},
            h('caption', {}, `Reported incidents per 1,000 students${v.category?.trim() ? `: ${v.category.trim()}` : ''}. Enrollment ${r.enrollment!.toLocaleString('en-US')}.`),
            h('thead', {}, h('tr', {}, h('th', { scope: 'col' }, 'Year'), h('th', { scope: 'col' }, 'Reported'), h('th', { scope: 'col' }, 'Per 1,000'))),
            h('tbody', {}, ...r.rows.map((x) => h('tr', {},
              h('th', { scope: 'row' }, x.label),
              h('td', {}, x.count.toLocaleString('en-US')),
              h('td', {}, formatRate(x.rate)),
            ))),
          )),
          list(r.rows.filter((x) => x.note).map((x) => `${x.label}: ${x.note}`)),
          r.skipped.length ? h('p', { class: 'small' }, `Left out (no count entered): ${r.skipped.join(', ')}.`) : null,
          r.warnings.length ? h('h4', {}, 'Check before using') : null,
          list(r.warnings, 'tool-flags'),
          h('p', { class: 'small' }, 'Reported incidents depend on reporting, and Clery counts cover a defined geography. Do not compare these rates across institutions.'),
        );
        text.textContent = ratesReport(r, v.category?.trim());
        out.hidden = false;
      };
      form.addEventListener('input', run);
      form.addEventListener('submit', (e) => { e.preventDefault(); run(); });
      form.addEventListener('reset', () => setTimeout(run));
      run();
    }
  </script>
</Base>
